# What reaches the Docker build daemon. The context is the repository root
# (see the header of `apps/api/Dockerfile` for why), so this file is what keeps
# that from meaning "upload everything".
#
# Secrets never enter the repo, and they never enter an image layer either
# (`AC-OPS-02.6`). `.env` is gitignored, but a `docker build` uploads the
# *directory*, not the commit — the same reason `.vercelignore` repeats the
# exclusion. Third lock on the same door.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github

# Virtualenvs are platform-specific and enormous; the image builds its own from
# `uv.lock`. `apps/api/.venv` in particular is a Windows venv on this machine
# and would poison a Linux image.
.venv
apps/api/.venv

# The web client is built and hosted separately (Vercel today, Cloudflare Pages
# per `15-infra-and-ops.md` §2). None of it belongs in the API image.
apps/web
apps/mobile
packages

# `docs/spec/ai-budget.yaml` is the one exception: `app/ai/budget.py` reads it
# at import time. Everything else under `docs/` is product decisions with no
# runtime role, so it is excluded and the Dockerfile copies the single file
# back in by name.
docs/adr
docs/compliance
docs/runbooks
docs/spec/*.md
docs/spec/*.json
docs/spec/*.py
docs/*.md

# The spec tooling and the operational scripts run in CI and on a workstation,
# never in the runtime image.
infra
apps/api/tests

# Build caches and local artifacts.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
node_modules
**/node_modules
.vite
**/dist

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea
*.swp
